    "markingSchemeEn": "(a) 4 marks — one per step, in order and with substance. A reversed order caps at 2; omitting follow-up loses 1.\n(b) 3 marks — one per cause, each at a different level; noting the limits of the paradox can recover one mark otherwise lost.\n(c) 2 marks — a specific advantage and cost (1); an improvement preserving both control and immediacy, such as tiered authority (1). \"Relax the rule\" without a mechanism earns nothing.\nThe marks shown are a practice scale used on this platform, not an HKEAA mark allocation. The reference answer lists the required steps and criteria rather than a copyable model script. Compare your own work against it point by point; nothing here is machine-marked.",
